{"id": "unknown-2026-09-25-009", "date": "2026-09-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "A Bangladesh merchandiser’s take: Sourcing gets more complex", "content": "US tariffs and Section 301 duties add paperwork and planning complexity, including product life cycle disclosure.\nBangladesh's February 2026 deal sets the tariff at 19 per cent, after 20 per cent from August 2025 and a proposed 37 per cent.\nZero-duty access covers only apparel using US cotton or man-made fibre within a volume still being finalised; EU-bound programmes keep Chinese inputs.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/a-bangladesh-merchandiser-s-take-sourcing-gets-more-complex-313777-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-25-010", "date": "2026-09-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["loss", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "ICE cotton gains on US export sales; harvest pressure persists", "content": "ICE December 2026 cotton settled 42 points higher at 83.31 cents per pound, its third gain this week after recent sharp losses.\nUS Upland cotton net sales rose to 230,517 bales in the week ended September 17, supporting futures as harvest supplies advance.\nChina reserve auctions showed strong uptake, but softer domestic spot indices and lower crude oil may limit cotton’s recovery.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-gains-on-us-export-sales-harvest-pressure-persists-313763-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-25-011", "date": "2026-09-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["warning", "delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Bangladesh sets up five panels to strengthen trade logistics", "content": "Bangladesh has set up five working groups to put the National Logistics Policy 2025 into action for trade and supply-chain efficiency.\nThe panels cover digitalisation, investment, skills, multimodal infrastructure and trade facilitation, areas critical to apparel exports.\nThe move follows warnings that high logistics costs and port delays are hurting competitiveness.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-sets-up-five-panels-to-strengthen-trade-logistics-313754-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-25-012", "date": "2026-09-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India’s FY27 growth forecast raised to 7.1% by OECD", "content": "India’s economy is projected to grow by 7.1 per cent in FY2026-27, retaining the strongest G20 outlook after an OECD forecast upgrade. \nUS growth is forecast at 2.2 per cent in 2026, China’s at 4.5 per cent and global growth at 2.9 per cent.\nHigher energy costs, trade uncertainty and inflation remained risks, while resilient domestic demand  supported India’s economic momentum. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-fy27-growth-forecast-raised-to-7-1-by-oecd-313729-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-25-013", "date": "2026-09-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Can Indonesia keep importing $4.56 bn of fabric for $8.7 bn apparel?", "content": "Indonesia imported $4.56 billion of fabric in 2025 and exported $801 million, leaving a $3.76 billion deficit.\nApparel exports reached $8.70 billion against $665 million of imports, generating an $8.04 billion surplus, with the US buying 56.4 per cent.\nJakarta is considering state-backed textile capacity, but mills must compete on price, quality, specifications and delivery.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/can-indonesia-keep-importing-4-56-bn-of-fabric-for-8-7-bn-apparel--313760-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-25-014", "date": "2026-09-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["[否定]growth", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh Bank keeps rate unchanged at 9.5% amid inflation pressure", "content": "Bangladesh Bank has kept its policy interest rate unchanged at 9.5 per cent as it assesses domestic and global shocks affecting inflation and growth. \nThe MPC noted easing headline inflation but flagged risks from Middle East conflicts, higher fuel prices and the new national pay scale. \nFor textile and apparel supply chains, borrowing costs remain unchanged while energy volatility stays a key risk.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-bank-keeps-rate-unchanged-at-9-5-amid-inflation-pressure-313755-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-25-015", "date": "2026-09-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Luxury demand polarises: How is the fashion supply chain responding?", "content": "First-half 2026 results show luxury demand concentrating at the top end as higher prices and softer discretionary spending curb aspirational buyers.\nPrada Group revenue rose 16 per cent at constant exchange rates to €3.048 billion (~$3.46 billion), while Hermès grew 6.1 per cent.\nMoncler EMEA, Ferragamo wholesale and Gucci show pressure, prompting reassessment of pricing, product mix and distribution.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/luxury-demand-polarises-how-is-the-fashion-supply-chain-responding--313753-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
